  "title": "Fin manifolds and their doubles count colourings: explicit S3 and dihedral constructions",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into finite nonabelian groups",
  "conclusion": "Handlebodies with tori attached along a planar graph turn counting maps into S3 into a spin model that recovers 3-colourings, and their closed doubles count pairs of colourings, 2 P(G,9)/3^|V|, with analogous chromatic formulas for most dihedral groups, Q8 and A4. The resulting #P-hardness is a case of Galindo's 2026 Turaev-Viro dichotomy; the explicit chromatic constructions are the contribution.",
